{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274833-hitting-but-getting-zero-extra-successes","id":1274833,"title":"Hitting but getting zero extra successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-16T21:21:56-08:00","id":1274833,"title":"Hitting but getting zero extra successes","content":"What happens if a PC is fighting somebody and scores enough successes to beat the target\u2019s defense but no more.<br /> <br /> Target has a defense of 2 and I roll 2 successes to attack them. I have zero successes to spend on the inflict injury stunt and assuming I\u2019m not using an automatic weapon then I can\u2019t pay for any stunts so the attack does nothing, but isn\u2019t a failure so I get no momentum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T23:39:35-08:00","id":1274844,"title":"","content":"By RAW, nothing happens. You hit but it does nothing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d be tempted to introduce a house rule that a \u2018successful\u2019 roll that needs to spend leftover successes to have any effect, but doesn\u2019t have any leftover to spend, earns one Momentum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T03:09:21-08:00","id":1274854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274833-hitting-but-getting-zero-extra-successes?p=1274844#post1274844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, nothing happens. You hit but it does nothing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d be tempted to introduce a house rule that a \u2018successful\u2019 roll that needs to spend leftover successes to have any effect, but doesn\u2019t have any leftover to spend, earns one Momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm thinking that in that circumstance you could inflict a light status condition on the opponent, but I suppose giving a Momentum can also work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T07:57:37-08:00","id":1274888,"title":"","content":"I'd grant a consolation for it, most likely Momentum. It works narratively, since you could be seen as softening up the opponent or searching for a weak spot in their defenses. It also takes a way the sting of succeeding but having no effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T08:33:18-08:00","id":1274892,"title":"","content":"According to the combat roll example on p. 101 this is actually a miss. But I'm trying to get that clarified by the devs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24507-baladain","name":"Baladain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-17T18:47:58-08:00","id":1274994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274833-hitting-but-getting-zero-extra-successes?p=1274844#post1274844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By RAW, nothing happens. You hit but it does nothing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d be tempted to introduce a house rule that a \u2018successful\u2019 roll that needs to spend leftover successes to have any effect, but doesn\u2019t have any leftover to spend, earns one Momentum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think based on my read by RAW, if the target had no soft armor and if the attack was a Close Combat attack they could use Inflict Damage because it costs successes equal to the amount of soft armor. <br /> <br /> I do find it confusing that close combat Inflict Damage appears to cost zero+armor while ranged and thrown costs 1+armor and all three cost 0+armor in Scion. I know some of the differences between the two variants of Storypath are to address the differences in theme, but this is an example of where playing more than one Storypath game is going to be frustrating because there are these little differences between fundamental building blocks of the core rules which are supposed to be the same underlying set of rules. We are interested in both Trinity and Scion, but I have a hard enough time getting my players to learn rules...they will never keep these differences straight and that is going to frustrate them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T01:34:37-08:00","id":1275041,"title":"","content":"I looked closer at both games. I think the difference between the 2 games is in Trinity all weapons have an enhancement bonus\u2014even fists. In Scion weapons are 0 unless tags increase it. This means barring armor that hitting defense with 0 extra successes means you actually can buy an inflict injury stunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T08:44:53-08:00","id":1275086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werlynn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274833-hitting-but-getting-zero-extra-successes?p=1275041#post1275041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked closer at both games. I think the difference between the 2 games is in Trinity all weapons have an enhancement bonus\u2014even fists. In Scion weapons are 0 unless tags increase it. This means barring armor that hitting defense with 0 extra successes means you actually can buy an inflict injury stunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can see that. Do we know if Trinity Close Combat's Inflict Damage only costing the opponent's armor as opposed to 1 + opponent's armor is an error? <br /> <br /> Forgot about the auto-enhancement on weapons in Trinity. Once a couple Storypath games are finalized and released it might be worth it for someone to put together a cheat guide for differences in the implementation of the core Storypath system between the different games. Differences bound up in the different types of character templates I have no problem keeping track of, but there are a bunch of little differences in the core game mechanics (like weapons in trinity having +1 enhancement while weapons in Scion not and some weapon or combat tags/stunts having different costs or different effects but the same names) that could be easily overlooked and might throw things off when switching from one game to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-18T14:13:31-08:00","id":1275164,"title":"","content":"It doesn't need to be an error. The 1 free enhancement doesn't let you buy a second injury <i>on its</i> own, but it does let you do fancy unarmed combat tricks which seems appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24935-werlynn","name":"werlynn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T05:36:38-08:00","id":1275270,"title":"","content":"I've brought this thread to the developers' collective attention, and we'll roll it into the errata. I'm pretty sure all instances of Inflict Damage should be zero cost, but it was a late-stage change, so it's possible the team missed a couple things. I'll chat with them about it. Thanks for bringing it up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T13:03:22-08:00","id":1275362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eddyfate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1274833-hitting-but-getting-zero-extra-successes?p=1275270#post1275270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've brought this thread to the developers' collective attention, and we'll roll it into the errata. I'm pretty sure all instances of Inflict Damage should be zero cost, but it was a late-stage change, so it's possible the team missed a couple things. I'll chat with them about it. Thanks for bringing it up!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks Eddy. This 0-cost interpretation is supported by Core p. 124 - &quot;The first benefit is soft armor. Typically, after a character has successfully struck another, <i>they can automatically inflict damage by purchasing the \u201cInflict Damage\u201d Stunt. Soft armor forces the at-tacker to spend additional successes</i> (equal to the rating of the armor) to cause injury.&quot; <br /> <br /> (Emphasis by me)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}